1
00:00:01,084 --> 00:00:03,044
<i>- Get out!</i>
<i>- No!</i>

2
00:00:03,128 --> 00:00:04,879
<i>- If you don't leave…</i>
<i>- What?</i>

3
00:00:04,963 --> 00:00:06,131
<i>I'm calling…</i>

4
00:00:06,214 --> 00:00:07,465
<i>Who? The cops?</i>

5
00:00:07,549 --> 00:00:10,427
<i>- Don't touch me! Get off me!</i>
<i>- You'll call the cops?</i>

6
00:00:10,510 --> 00:00:11,928
<i>- You bastard!</i>
- [BLOW LANDS]

7
00:00:12,721 --> 00:00:15,015
[JORDAN GROANS]

8
00:00:17,475 --> 00:00:19,436
<i>I only got my hopes up</i>

9
00:00:20,812 --> 00:00:22,814
<i>because I felt like…</i>

10
00:00:24,816 --> 00:00:26,276
<i>he was all I had left.</i>

11
00:00:29,112 --> 00:00:30,113
<i>Mom is dead.</i>

12
00:00:31,281 --> 00:00:32,991
<i>Grandpa Jude…</i>

13
00:00:33,074 --> 00:00:35,577
<i>He's still alive,</i>
<i>but it's like he's not even here.</i>

14
00:00:36,161 --> 00:00:37,829
<i>It's just hard to accept…</i>

15
00:00:39,664 --> 00:00:41,499
<i>that he's the only family I have left.</i>

16
00:00:42,167 --> 00:00:43,626
<i>And this is what happens.</i>

17
00:00:44,961 --> 00:00:48,631
<i>Why did I have to have</i>
<i>such a terrible father?</i>

18
00:00:51,134 --> 00:00:52,927
<i>But you're not like him.</i>

19
00:00:55,138 --> 00:00:56,431
<i>Right?</i>

20
00:00:57,390 --> 00:00:59,893
<i>You're nothing like your father.</i>

21
00:01:00,602 --> 00:01:03,354
<i>Because you are better than him.</i>

22
00:01:03,438 --> 00:01:06,733
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC PLAYING]

23
00:01:06,816 --> 00:01:11,780
<i>And it's not true that</i>
<i>he's the only one you have left.</i>

24
00:01:12,822 --> 00:01:14,699
<i>That you don't have</i>
<i>anyone on your side anymore.</i>

25
00:01:19,662 --> 00:01:21,164
<i>I'm here.</i>

26
00:01:21,247 --> 00:01:28,213
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

27
00:01:33,218 --> 00:01:40,225
["AAMININ" BY JAMES REID
AND KATHRYN BERNARDO PLAYING]

28
00:01:43,895 --> 00:01:45,313
[JORDAN SIGHS SHARPLY]

29
00:01:48,441 --> 00:01:55,406
["AAMININ" CONTINUES]

30
00:02:19,347 --> 00:02:26,271
["AAMININ" CONTINUES]

31
00:02:35,363 --> 00:02:36,781
[JORDAN EXHALES DEEPLY]

32
00:02:38,783 --> 00:02:40,869
[JORDAN SNIFFLES]

33
00:02:40,952 --> 00:02:42,162
<i>Um…</i>

34
00:02:48,251 --> 00:02:49,335
[BILLY CLEARS THROAT]

35
00:02:51,421 --> 00:02:52,755
<i>No, I did.</i>

36
00:02:53,882 --> 00:02:54,924
<i>Dude.</i>

37
00:02:56,426 --> 00:02:59,762
<i>I think it's time</i>
<i>for you to know the truth.</i>

38
00:02:59,846 --> 00:03:06,019
["AAMININ" CONTINUES]

39
00:03:08,855 --> 00:03:10,607
<i>I'm so in love with you.</i>

40
00:03:10,690 --> 00:03:17,697
["AAMININ" CONTINUES]

41
00:03:20,408 --> 00:03:22,327
<i>What are you trying to say?</i>

42
00:03:25,663 --> 00:03:26,623
<i>Billy.</i>

43
00:03:28,666 --> 00:03:30,209
<i>I love you.</i>

44
00:03:31,044 --> 00:03:33,421
<i>I think you need to rest.</i>
<i>You should rest up.</i>

45
00:03:36,841 --> 00:03:38,176
<i>- Billy.</i>
<i>- I have to go.</i>

46
00:03:44,224 --> 00:03:46,184
[MUSIC FADES]

47
00:03:49,646 --> 00:03:55,235
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

48
00:03:56,236 --> 00:03:57,904
[JORDAN, BILLY COUGH]

49
00:03:57,987 --> 00:03:59,280
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

50
00:03:59,364 --> 00:04:01,074
<i>Oliver! Oliver?</i>

51
00:04:01,157 --> 00:04:02,659
<i>They're okay now. It's okay.</i>

52
00:04:02,742 --> 00:04:03,993
<i>Billy.</i>

53
00:04:04,077 --> 00:04:05,203
<i>We'll follow them.</i>

54
00:04:05,912 --> 00:04:07,872
<i>- Okay.</i>
<i>- It's okay.</i>

55
00:04:07,956 --> 00:04:09,249
[VOICE TREMBLING] <i>Okay.</i>

56
00:04:09,332 --> 00:04:10,625
<i>I'll make it up to you.</i>

57
00:04:10,708 --> 00:04:11,960
<i>Too late!</i>

58
00:04:12,043 --> 00:04:14,003
<i>Sure, you're back! But it's too late!</i>

59
00:04:14,087 --> 00:04:15,546
<i>You can't change anything now!</i>

60
00:04:15,630 --> 00:04:17,799
<i>- Nothing at all!</i>
- [ENRICO GROANS]

61
00:04:18,424 --> 00:04:19,300
<i>Dad?</i>

62
00:04:19,384 --> 00:04:21,511
- [RAGGED BREATHS]
<i>- Papa?</i>

63
00:04:21,594 --> 00:04:22,512
<i>Guys.</i>

64
00:04:22,595 --> 00:04:25,848
<i>The company is</i>
<i>literally bleeding right now.</i>

65
00:04:27,350 --> 00:04:29,477
<i>Where's your commitment to your work?</i>

66
00:04:29,560 --> 00:04:30,770
<i>Billy.</i>

67
00:04:32,438 --> 00:04:33,690
<i>Billy, I'm begging you.</i>

68
00:04:33,773 --> 00:04:36,776
<i>If you drop the case against my mom,</i>

69
00:04:36,859 --> 00:04:39,654
<i>I promise I'll watch over her.</i>

70
00:04:39,737 --> 00:04:41,990
<i>I promise she won't bother you.</i>

71
00:04:42,073 --> 00:04:46,744
<i>I promise, Billy. Please.</i>
<i>Just withdraw the case against my mother.</i>

72
00:04:46,828 --> 00:04:47,912
<i>Please, Billy. Please.</i>

73
00:04:47,996 --> 00:04:49,580
<i>Have mercy on my mother. Please.</i>

74
00:04:49,664 --> 00:04:51,374
<i>Dad came to visit me.</i>

75
00:04:53,710 --> 00:04:55,086
<i>He apologized to me.</i>

76
00:04:57,547 --> 00:05:00,883
<i>It turns out he was in jail all this time.</i>

77
00:05:00,967 --> 00:05:02,302
<i>So he was released from jail?</i>

78
00:05:02,385 --> 00:05:04,012
<i>He broke out</i>

79
00:05:04,095 --> 00:05:05,346
<i>with Caloy.</i>

80
00:05:05,430 --> 00:05:06,347
<i>What?!</i>

81
00:05:06,431 --> 00:05:07,640
<i>Dude.</i>

82
00:05:09,017 --> 00:05:12,395
<i>I think it's time</i>
<i>for you to know the truth.</i>

83
00:05:16,649 --> 00:05:17,984
<i>I'm so in love with you.</i>

84
00:05:18,067 --> 00:05:21,446
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

85
00:05:21,529 --> 00:05:23,740
[PHONE ALARM RINGING]

86
00:05:25,408 --> 00:05:26,534
Billy.

87
00:05:28,619 --> 00:05:29,954
- Billy.
- [GASPS]

88
00:05:31,122 --> 00:05:33,875
Your phone alarm has been ringing nonstop.

89
00:05:33,958 --> 00:05:35,335
I'm sorry, Auntie.

90
00:05:37,170 --> 00:05:39,630
Why don't you take the day off?

91
00:05:39,714 --> 00:05:41,340
I can't, Auntie.

92
00:05:42,216 --> 00:05:44,427
Your father's heart is already recovering.

93
00:05:44,510 --> 00:05:47,388
Now, it seems yours is the one
that needs attention.

94
00:05:48,431 --> 00:05:51,059
- My heart is tough, Auntie.
- [PRECIOUS] Hmm.

95
00:05:51,142 --> 00:05:55,396
Yes, your heart might be tough,
but what about Jordan's heart?

96
00:05:55,480 --> 00:05:56,939
How is he doing?

97
00:05:57,023 --> 00:05:59,442
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

98
00:05:59,525 --> 00:06:00,651
What about you, Auntie Pres?

99
00:06:00,735 --> 00:06:05,406
Did you notice he had feelings for me?

100
00:06:05,490 --> 00:06:07,200
No, I didn't.

101
00:06:07,283 --> 00:06:10,495
That's why I was surprised
when you told me last night.

102
00:06:10,578 --> 00:06:15,374
But, Billy, you're both
going through a lot right now.

103
00:06:15,958 --> 00:06:19,545
You should be there for each other.

104
00:06:20,546 --> 00:06:23,549
Talk to him. Call him and check on him.

105
00:06:23,633 --> 00:06:26,594
I don't know how to face him right now.

106
00:06:29,889 --> 00:06:31,933
I don't know how.

107
00:06:34,352 --> 00:06:37,021
What's that medicine for?

108
00:06:38,981 --> 00:06:39,857
It's nothing, Auntie.

109
00:06:39,941 --> 00:06:42,902
I just had a hard time
sleeping last night.

110
00:06:43,820 --> 00:06:45,404
But I'm okay.

111
00:06:45,488 --> 00:06:47,949
All right then. We're leaving now.

112
00:06:48,032 --> 00:06:51,244
Auntie, you don't have
to face Mariela, okay?

113
00:06:51,327 --> 00:06:54,622
If you want, I can go with Dad instead.

114
00:06:54,705 --> 00:06:55,790
Oh, come on now.

115
00:06:55,873 --> 00:06:58,459
You're already having trouble sleeping.

116
00:06:58,543 --> 00:07:00,044
I can handle it.

117
00:07:00,128 --> 00:07:05,174
And besides, I don't have to see
and talk to Mariela.

118
00:07:05,258 --> 00:07:09,720
I'm just there to assist your father.

119
00:07:11,681 --> 00:07:14,392
Don't stress yourself out more, okay?

120
00:07:14,475 --> 00:07:16,644
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

121
00:07:17,270 --> 00:07:18,938
All right. I'll go now.

122
00:07:19,021 --> 00:07:20,356
Mwah.

123
00:07:20,440 --> 00:07:21,858
Get some rest.

124
00:07:23,025 --> 00:07:28,781
[GENTLE MUSIC CONTINUES]

125
00:07:31,576 --> 00:07:34,954
- JORDAN: IT'S ALL GOOD NOW, DUDE.
- BILLY: OKAY. THANK YOU, DUDE.

126
00:07:35,037 --> 00:07:38,791
JORDAN: NO PROBLEM, ANYTHING
FOR YOU. GET SOME REST.

127
00:07:51,888 --> 00:07:57,894
[GENTLE MUSIC CONTINUES]

128
00:07:59,312 --> 00:08:05,693
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

129
00:09:04,335 --> 00:09:06,295
[BIRDS CHIRPING]

130
00:09:06,379 --> 00:09:08,381
So, I was thinking,

131
00:09:08,464 --> 00:09:11,467
we should just go back
to featuring couples

132
00:09:11,551 --> 00:09:13,678
to remind everyone

133
00:09:13,761 --> 00:09:18,391
that LoveList is still about
helping people find real love.

134
00:09:18,474 --> 00:09:20,351
The right kind of love.

135
00:09:21,018 --> 00:09:22,019
[TONI] Hmm…

136
00:09:22,687 --> 00:09:24,230
Can you share with the group

137
00:09:24,313 --> 00:09:27,149
which interesting couple
you want to feature?

138
00:09:28,109 --> 00:09:29,610
Um…

139
00:09:29,694 --> 00:09:33,155
Do you know that trending
bakery in Cavite?

140
00:09:33,990 --> 00:09:35,908
Its owner is a LoveLister.

141
00:09:35,992 --> 00:09:38,619
And the person they matched with
on our app

142
00:09:38,703 --> 00:09:40,580
is their childhood best friend!

143
00:09:40,663 --> 00:09:42,790
- [BLAIRE] Really?!
- [JORDAN COUGHING]

144
00:09:42,873 --> 00:09:45,251
Yes, they're best friends.

145
00:09:45,334 --> 00:09:48,504
At first, they were just
teasing each other.

146
00:09:48,588 --> 00:09:50,548
But the revelation is,

147
00:09:50,631 --> 00:09:53,884
the bakery owner has had a long-time crush
on their best friend.

148
00:09:53,968 --> 00:09:56,304
- How sweet!
- [CHARM] Right?

149
00:09:56,387 --> 00:09:58,973
- [BLAIRE] That's so endearing!
- [JORDAN CLEARS THROAT]

150
00:09:59,724 --> 00:10:01,475
What do you think, chief?

151
00:10:02,059 --> 00:10:03,269
It's okay.

152
00:10:04,145 --> 00:10:06,647
Let's just make sure

153
00:10:06,731 --> 00:10:09,025
that they'd be comfortable
having their story featured.

154
00:10:09,692 --> 00:10:12,194
- [CHARM] Yes! Okay! Let's do this!
- [TONI GIGGLES]

155
00:10:12,278 --> 00:10:14,822
- [BLAIRE] I'm excited!
- [BILLY] Okay, let's wrap up this meeting?

156
00:10:14,905 --> 00:10:16,532
- Okay!
- [BLAIRE] Okay.

157
00:10:16,616 --> 00:10:17,491
[TONI] Excuse me.

158
00:10:17,575 --> 00:10:19,493
- [JORDAN CLEARS THROAT]
- [BLAIRE] Thanks.

159
00:10:37,261 --> 00:10:41,098
[MUSIC BUILDS]

160
00:10:41,182 --> 00:10:42,350
Let's talk.

161
00:10:42,433 --> 00:10:49,315
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

162
00:10:50,816 --> 00:10:52,401
[MUSIC FADES]

163
00:11:10,127 --> 00:11:11,921
We looked so stupid earlier.

164
00:11:15,758 --> 00:11:17,009
Are you okay now?

165
00:11:22,139 --> 00:11:24,350
Billy, I know last night
wasn't the best time

166
00:11:24,433 --> 00:11:26,185
for me to tell you my feelings, but…

167
00:11:30,106 --> 00:11:32,108
what I said was true.

168
00:11:32,191 --> 00:11:35,277
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

169
00:11:35,361 --> 00:11:36,654
Since when?

170
00:11:42,868 --> 00:11:43,953
At first,

171
00:11:44,912 --> 00:11:50,209
I was confused about how I really felt.

172
00:11:55,172 --> 00:11:57,883
We've grown to know each other
very well, Billy.

173
00:12:02,096 --> 00:12:03,389
Just one look,

174
00:12:05,224 --> 00:12:06,976
and I already know what you're thinking.

175
00:12:09,395 --> 00:12:11,105
I know which smile is real.

176
00:12:13,399 --> 00:12:17,570
I know when you're pissed off
and just pretending to be okay.

177
00:12:20,781 --> 00:12:22,074
You're a strong woman…

178
00:12:24,577 --> 00:12:27,496
but you're scared of mice.

179
00:12:29,123 --> 00:12:31,333
You hate it when people are late.

180
00:12:31,417 --> 00:12:33,002
You overthink everything.

181
00:12:33,836 --> 00:12:35,463
You think about everyone.

182
00:12:37,214 --> 00:12:38,716
As your best friend,

183
00:12:40,009 --> 00:12:41,844
I've learned a lot about you.

184
00:12:46,515 --> 00:12:48,184
I didn't mean to, but…

185
00:12:52,938 --> 00:12:55,608
suddenly, I stopped
memorizing your habits.

186
00:12:58,611 --> 00:13:00,070
I started loving them.

187
00:13:05,784 --> 00:13:08,621
I fell in love with all of it.

188
00:13:11,999 --> 00:13:13,459
I fell in love with you.

189
00:13:14,251 --> 00:13:21,133
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

190
00:13:22,176 --> 00:13:23,344
Thank you.

191
00:13:29,600 --> 00:13:32,269
Thank you for being honest with me.

192
00:13:34,355 --> 00:13:35,731
[CHUCKLES WRYLY]

193
00:13:37,066 --> 00:13:38,234
Ouch.

194
00:13:40,319 --> 00:13:42,154
I just told you I love you, and…

195
00:13:44,031 --> 00:13:45,574
your response was "Thank you."

196
00:13:45,658 --> 00:13:47,243
- Sorry.
- That hurts.

197
00:13:47,326 --> 00:13:49,495
Stop being silly.

198
00:13:49,578 --> 00:13:50,913
I mean, why me?

199
00:13:50,996 --> 00:13:53,249
[BREATHES DEEPLY]

200
00:13:54,542 --> 00:13:56,835
So much is going on right now.

201
00:14:01,048 --> 00:14:02,591
Why now?

202
00:14:06,428 --> 00:14:07,555
Wait, if…

203
00:14:09,098 --> 00:14:11,642
if our lives weren't so chaotic right now,

204
00:14:11,725 --> 00:14:14,770
what, I… I could stand a chance?

205
00:14:17,314 --> 00:14:18,357
Billy.

206
00:14:21,944 --> 00:14:23,153
Are you worried?

207
00:14:23,988 --> 00:14:25,364
Is it LoveList?

208
00:14:26,866 --> 00:14:27,741
Oliver?

209
00:14:27,825 --> 00:14:29,910
- Jordan…
- Why?

210
00:14:34,373 --> 00:14:36,500
- Billy.
- It's too messy right now.

211
00:14:36,584 --> 00:14:38,669
I can't afford to love.

212
00:14:38,752 --> 00:14:39,837
Why?

213
00:14:41,005 --> 00:14:43,173
- Jordan--
- Just tell me why.

214
00:14:44,300 --> 00:14:45,509
I need to know.

215
00:14:51,140 --> 00:14:52,141
Billy.

216
00:14:55,102 --> 00:14:56,437
You know what?

217
00:15:01,108 --> 00:15:02,359
What?

218
00:15:06,572 --> 00:15:10,784
So many people who I loved deeply

219
00:15:11,702 --> 00:15:13,329
have come and gone.

220
00:15:14,663 --> 00:15:17,082
Whether they meant it or not,

221
00:15:18,292 --> 00:15:19,960
they hurt me.

222
00:15:20,920 --> 00:15:22,254
And you know that.

223
00:15:23,756 --> 00:15:26,425
You know what I realized after all that?

224
00:15:27,426 --> 00:15:28,719
[SIGHS]

225
00:15:31,680 --> 00:15:33,223
If someone hurts you,

226
00:15:33,307 --> 00:15:35,726
no matter how much they try
to make it up to you

227
00:15:35,809 --> 00:15:37,603
or how many times they apologize…

228
00:15:39,688 --> 00:15:42,024
nothing will be the same.

229
00:15:43,317 --> 00:15:48,364
[GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]

230
00:15:48,447 --> 00:15:51,492
You know, sometimes I wish there was

231
00:15:51,575 --> 00:15:54,161
a reset button I could click…

232
00:15:56,455 --> 00:15:58,165
that'd give me a clean slate
or a fresh start.

233
00:15:58,248 --> 00:16:00,793
A button that could make me
forget about everything.

234
00:16:04,171 --> 00:16:05,464
But there's no such thing.

235
00:16:08,342 --> 00:16:15,265
[GLOOMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

236
00:16:17,267 --> 00:16:19,812
Sometimes, it doesn't matter
how strong your relationship is.

237
00:16:22,815 --> 00:16:25,025
If you hurt each other,
nothing can fix it.

238
00:16:32,825 --> 00:16:35,744
And I don't want that
to happen to us, Jordan.

239
00:16:43,127 --> 00:16:45,963
I don't want to ruin what we have.

240
00:16:52,136 --> 00:16:53,929
I couldn't bear it.

241
00:16:55,180 --> 00:17:02,021
["AAMININ" BY JAMES REID
AND KATHRYN BERNARDO PLAYING]

242
00:17:11,238 --> 00:17:12,781
[SIGHS DEEPLY]

243
00:17:14,408 --> 00:17:15,576
Got it.

244
00:17:20,748 --> 00:17:21,915
Um…

245
00:17:23,709 --> 00:17:26,045
Billy, I… I respect your decision.

246
00:17:32,134 --> 00:17:33,218
Okay.

247
00:17:35,512 --> 00:17:37,556
But can we really just act

248
00:17:38,849 --> 00:17:41,518
like nothing happened?

249
00:17:51,820 --> 00:17:54,198
Can you forget that I love you?

250
00:18:01,080 --> 00:18:03,123
Because I can't.

251
00:18:10,881 --> 00:18:13,342
I'm sorry. I didn't mean to love you.

252
00:18:14,635 --> 00:18:21,266
["AAMININ" CONTINUES]

253
00:18:47,960 --> 00:18:49,336
That might be your last.

254
00:18:51,088 --> 00:18:52,631
I'll take a few days off.

255
00:18:56,093 --> 00:18:57,386
I just need time to…

256
00:18:59,888 --> 00:19:01,390
take everything in.

257
00:19:02,891 --> 00:19:04,143
What happened with Dad

258
00:19:05,561 --> 00:19:08,188
and your rejection.

259
00:19:09,231 --> 00:19:10,524
Hey!

260
00:19:10,607 --> 00:19:17,573
["AAMININ" CONTINUES]

261
00:19:28,083 --> 00:19:29,418
I'll miss you.

262
00:19:34,631 --> 00:19:35,883
As you should.

263
00:19:40,512 --> 00:19:46,435
["AAMININ" CONTINUES]

264
00:19:46,518 --> 00:19:48,145
[MUSIC FADES]

265
00:19:50,439 --> 00:19:53,317
Don't worry about our daughter.

266
00:19:54,568 --> 00:19:56,945
She's looking for a job.

267
00:19:57,029 --> 00:19:59,031
She's trying to start over.

268
00:20:01,241 --> 00:20:03,368
[MARIELA] How about me?

269
00:20:04,161 --> 00:20:06,496
- [UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]
- I want to start over too.

270
00:20:10,417 --> 00:20:11,710
Mariela.

271
00:20:13,462 --> 00:20:15,172
You have to get better first.

272
00:20:15,756 --> 00:20:17,841
Because you've hurt other people.

273
00:20:18,842 --> 00:20:21,220
You're even hurting yourself.

274
00:20:22,846 --> 00:20:25,474
You decided to let Bea go.

275
00:20:26,683 --> 00:20:28,310
Can't you do the same for me?

276
00:20:29,186 --> 00:20:31,647
What you did to Billy is no small thing.

277
00:20:35,525 --> 00:20:38,570
So, it's Billy's decision
to lock me up in here.

278
00:20:39,905 --> 00:20:42,407
Mariela, you have committed a grave crime.

279
00:20:43,533 --> 00:20:45,911
You must pay for it.

280
00:20:46,536 --> 00:20:49,623
Says who? Your mistress?

281
00:20:50,791 --> 00:20:53,252
That Precious is making you
do this, isn't she?

282
00:20:53,335 --> 00:20:55,796
Precious has nothing to do with this.

283
00:20:56,922 --> 00:20:58,340
Do you love her?

284
00:20:58,423 --> 00:21:03,387
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

285
00:21:03,470 --> 00:21:06,098
Do you love her more than me?

286
00:21:09,017 --> 00:21:10,227
[SOBS]

287
00:21:10,310 --> 00:21:16,566
Is there really no chance
for you to love me again?

288
00:21:20,279 --> 00:21:21,613
[SOBS]

289
00:21:25,784 --> 00:21:26,994
Mariela…

290
00:21:27,077 --> 00:21:29,204
It's not too late.

291
00:21:31,540 --> 00:21:35,460
It's time we were good parents to Bea.

292
00:21:36,336 --> 00:21:37,879
That's what matters.

293
00:21:37,963 --> 00:21:39,423
[MARIELA SNIFFLES]

294
00:21:42,467 --> 00:21:45,971
So get better. Take care of yourself.

295
00:21:49,599 --> 00:21:56,481
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

296
00:22:07,659 --> 00:22:11,163
[SNIFFLING]

297
00:22:13,165 --> 00:22:16,501
<i>Well, it shows here that</i>
<i>you have a criminal record.</i>

298
00:22:17,878 --> 00:22:21,798
<i>But that case is over.</i>
<i>It's been settled.</i>

299
00:22:21,882 --> 00:22:24,259
<i>I'm sorry. It's our company policy.</i>

300
00:22:24,343 --> 00:22:27,179
<i>How can I start over</i>
<i>if you won't give me a chance?</i>

301
00:22:27,262 --> 00:22:28,847
<i>"Policy" my ass!</i>

302
00:22:28,930 --> 00:22:31,600
<i>I want to kill your father's mistress!</i>

303
00:22:31,683 --> 00:22:34,394
<i>Seriously?! Could you</i>
<i>stop saying that?!</i>

304
00:22:34,478 --> 00:22:37,439
<i>Do you really want to get out of here?</i>
<i>Tell me, do you?</i>

305
00:22:37,522 --> 00:22:40,650
<i>Then stop saying you want</i>
<i>to kill people, Ma!</i>

306
00:22:40,734 --> 00:22:42,069
<i>We've already completed</i>

307
00:22:42,152 --> 00:22:44,154
<i>the second assessment of your mother.</i>

308
00:22:44,237 --> 00:22:46,406
<i>And she has made a huge improvement.</i>

309
00:22:47,032 --> 00:22:50,744
<i>She no longer exhibits psychotic symptoms</i>

310
00:22:50,827 --> 00:22:53,330
<i>or signs of mental incompetence.</i>

311
00:22:53,413 --> 00:22:55,290
<i>She's aware of what she's doing</i>

312
00:22:55,373 --> 00:22:57,542
<i>and the consequences of her actions.</i>

313
00:22:57,626 --> 00:23:01,213
<i>Her previous treatment really helped,</i>

314
00:23:01,296 --> 00:23:03,757
<i>along with the rehabilitation</i>
<i>that she underwent.</i>

315
00:23:07,803 --> 00:23:08,887
[SHRIEKS]

316
00:23:08,970 --> 00:23:12,516
<i>What? You just suddenly</i>
<i>decide to ghost me?</i>

317
00:23:15,685 --> 00:23:17,479
<i>Dino, I love you,</i>

318
00:23:17,562 --> 00:23:19,731
<i>but I don't want to throw away my life.</i>

319
00:23:19,815 --> 00:23:22,484
<i>The cops just interrogated me.</i>
<i>You're gonna get me in trouble.</i>

320
00:23:22,567 --> 00:23:24,194
<i>No one's getting in trouble.</i>

321
00:23:24,778 --> 00:23:27,155
<i>We're leaving. I'll find us a new place.</i>

322
00:23:27,948 --> 00:23:31,076
<i>♪ I know you gave me your best ♪</i>

323
00:23:32,244 --> 00:23:35,580
<i>♪ Feels like you're a part of me ♪</i>

324
00:23:36,665 --> 00:23:42,671
<i>♪ I know it hurts</i>
<i>'Cause that shit hurt me too ♪</i>

325
00:23:42,754 --> 00:23:47,592
<i>♪ Oh, even all the greatest stories end ♪</i>

326
00:23:47,676 --> 00:23:50,470
<i>♪ And I would do it all again ♪</i>

327
00:23:50,554 --> 00:23:52,389
<i>I understand.</i>

328
00:23:52,472 --> 00:23:55,267
<i>You have to be there</i>
<i>for your other daughter.</i>

329
00:23:55,350 --> 00:23:57,811
<i>I'm just worried about your health.</i>

330
00:24:00,605 --> 00:24:02,190
<i>I'll take care of myself.</i>

331
00:24:03,984 --> 00:24:05,861
<i>- Dad?</i>
- [KNOCKS ON DOOR]

332
00:24:09,489 --> 00:24:10,699
<i>Auntie?</i>

333
00:24:12,450 --> 00:24:13,702
<i>What happened to your face?</i>
